{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And they rejoiced</b> — those who go down to the sea." "<b>For they grew quiet</b> — the waves." "<b>To the haven</b> — like גבול (boundary), and like it: לא חזו ימיו (Job 36:30), its meaning: they did not bound his days. And the sense: they cannot attain knowledge of the end of his days."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 107, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:02.069313860Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}